Complement: {comp_dna}&#34;) print(f&#34;Reverse complement: {comp_dna[::-1]}&#34;) # SOLUTION (uncomment to verify): # The bugs are: # 1. If you used &#39;DNA&#39; instead of &#39;dna&#39;, Python is case-sensitive # 2. range(0, len(dna), 2) skips odd positions -- try range(len(dna)) # 3. Using &#39;=&#39; instead of &#39;==&#39; in comparisons (though this example uses &#39;in&#39;)We examined TypeError, KeyError, IndexError, and ValueError &ndash; the four most common errors in bioinformatics scripts. Understanding error messages is half the debugging battle.
